From 20260720-dwc3-skip-init-quirk Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Krishna Kurapati <krishna.kurapati@xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 06:56:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: qcom: Add support to skip phy management by USB core

The Qualcomm DWC3 glue driver manages its PHYs itself.  If the USB core also
initializes the PHY, the extra init reference can keep the PHY's init count
nonzero during system suspend and prevent the Qualcomm glue driver's exit
operation from powering it down.

This is the reviewed upstream proposal from change-id
20260720-dwc3-skip-init-quirk-c110eae068ac, ported without changing its
behavior to Armada's Linux 7.2 package.  The xHCI platform driver already
supports the `xhci-skip-phy-init-quirk` software property in this base.

Link: https://lkml.iu.edu/2607.2/15543.html
Signed-off-by: Krishna Kurapati <krishna.kurapati@xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
index ac68b4218b56..ba26e61df915 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 #include <linux/usb/hcd.h>
 #include <linux/usb.h>
+#include <linux/property.h>
 #include "core.h"
 #include "glue.h"
 
 /* USB QSCRATCH Hardware registers */
@@ -419,6 +420,16 @@ static irqreturn_t qcom_dwc3_resume_irq(int irq, void *data)
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
 
+static int dwc3_qcom_set_swnode(struct device *dev)
+{
+	const struct property_entry props[] = {
+		PROPERTY_ENTRY_BOOL("xhci-skip-phy-init-quirk"),
+		{}
+	};
+
+	return device_create_managed_software_node(dev, props, NULL);
+}
+
 static void dwc3_qcom_select_utmi_clk(struct dwc3_qcom *qcom)
 {
 	/* Configure dwc3 to use UTMI clock as PIPE clock not present */
@@ -683,7 +694,11 @@ static int dwc3_qcom_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ignore_pipe_clk)
 		dwc3_qcom_select_utmi_clk(qcom);
 
+	ret = dwc3_qcom_set_swnode(dev);
+	if (ret)
+		goto clk_disable;
+
 	qcom->mode = usb_get_dr_mode(dev);
 
 	if (qcom->mode == USB_DR_MODE_HOST) {
 		qcom->current_role = USB_ROLE_HOST;
-- 
